            "finalAnswer": "## Rendering pipeline trace\n\n**1. React component → static-scene render function**\n\n`StaticCanvas` (`packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx:29`) is the React component. It's a `React.memo`-wrapped function component whose `useEffect` (line 33-81) calls `renderStaticScene(...)` (imported from `../../renderer/staticScene`) on every render where memoized props changed (per `areEqual`), passing the canvas element, roughjs canvas (`rc`), scale, elements, appState, and renderConfig.\n\n`renderStaticScene` (`renderer/staticScene.ts:470`) either calls the throttled version (`renderStaticSceneThrottled`, RAF-throttled) or `_renderStaticScene` directly. `_renderStaticScene` sets up the 2D context, draws the grid, then iterates `visibleElements` and calls `renderElement(element, elementsMap, allElementsMap, rc, context, renderConfig, appState)` (from `renderer/renderElement.ts`) for each one.\n\n**2. Where the roughjs shape comes from**\n\nInside `renderElement.ts`, before drawing, the code calls:\n```ts\nShapeCache.generateElementShape(element, renderConfig);\n```\n(`renderElement.ts:811`, also `:763` for freedraw). This is the seam that supplies the roughjs `Drawable`.\n\n`ShapeCache` (`packages/excalidraw/scene/ShapeCache.ts:13`) is a `WeakMap<ExcalidrawElement, ElementShape>` cache keyed by the element object itself:\n- `generateElementShape` first checks the cache (`ShapeCache.get(element)`) — if a shape is already cached (and we're not exporting, which always forces regeneration), it returns the cached shape immediately.\n- On a cache miss, it calls `_generateElementShape(element, ShapeCache.rg, renderConfig)` from `scene/Shape.ts`, where `ShapeCache.rg` is a single shared `RoughGenerator` instance (`new RoughGenerator()`, `ShapeCache.ts:14`).\n- `_generateElementShape` (`Shape.ts:306`) switches on `element.type` and calls the actual roughjs generator methods — e.g. `generator.rectangle(...)`/`generator.path(...)` for rectangles/embeddables with rounded corners, `generator.polygon(...)`/`generator.path(...)` for diamonds, `generator.ellipse(...)` for ellipses, `generator.linearPath`/`generator.polygon`/`generator.curve` for lines/arrows (plus arrowhead sub-shapes via `getArrowheadShapes`), and a `generator.curve` fill shape for closed freedraw paths. Options (stroke color, roughness, fill, dash pattern, seed, etc.) come from `generateRoughOptions(element)`, derived straight from the element's own style properties.\n- The resulting `Drawable` (or `Drawable[]`) is stored back in the cache via `ShapeCache.cache.set(element, shape)`.\n\n**3. Actually drawing it**\n\nOnce the shape exists in the cache, `drawElementOnCanvas` (`renderElement.ts:383`) retrieves it with `ShapeCache.get(element)!` and hands it to the roughjs canvas instance: `rc.draw(shape)` (single shapes for rectangle/diamond/ellipse, or a `.forEach(shape => rc.draw(shape))` loop for arrows/lines, which have multiple `Drawable`s — the path plus arrowhead shapes).\n\n**Summary of the chain:**\n`StaticCanvas` (React component) → `renderStaticScene`/`_renderStaticScene` (`renderer/staticScene.ts`) → `renderElement` (`renderer/renderElement.ts`) → `ShapeCache.generateElementShape` (`scene/ShapeCache.ts`, cache-or-generate via `_generateElementShape` in `scene/Shape.ts`, using a shared `RoughGenerator`) → `drawElementOnCanvas` reads the cached `Drawable` and calls `rc.draw(shape)`.",
