            "finalAnswer": "Verified against the source. Here's the trace:\n\n## 1. React component that triggers rendering\n\n**`StaticCanvas`** (`packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx`) is the component that draws elements to the canvas. It's mounted by `App.tsx:1728`. Inside it, a `useEffect` (no dependency array — runs every render to stay in sync) calls `renderStaticScene(...)` at `StaticCanvas.tsx:68`, passing the canvas, the roughjs `RoughCanvas` instance (`rc`), the elements map, `appState`, and render config.\n\n`renderStaticScene` (`renderer/staticScene.ts:470`) either throttles via `renderStaticSceneThrottled` or calls `_renderStaticScene` (`staticScene.ts:208`) directly. That function iterates `visibleElements.forEach(...)` and calls `renderElement(element, ...)` (`renderer/renderElement.ts:698`) per element.\n\n## 2. Where the roughjs shape comes from\n\n`renderElement.ts:811` (or `:763` for freedraw) calls `ShapeCache.generateElementShape(element, renderConfig)`. `ShapeCache` (`packages/excalidraw/scene/ShapeCache.ts`) keeps a `WeakMap<ExcalidrawElement, ElementShape>` keyed by the element object itself (line 15). On a cache miss, it calls `_generateElementShape` in `scene/Shape.ts:306`, which invokes the roughjs `RoughGenerator` methods (`.rectangle`, `.ellipse`, `.path`, `.line`, etc.) to actually build the `Drawable`(s), then stores the result in the WeakMap.\n\nThe element is then painted in `drawElementOnCanvas` (`renderElement.ts:383`), which pulls the *cached* shape back out via `ShapeCache.get(element)` (lines 398/406/417) and hands it to roughjs's own paint API, `rc.draw(shape)`.\n\n**Chain:** `App.tsx` → `<StaticCanvas>` → `useEffect` → `renderStaticScene` → `_renderStaticScene` (loops elements) → `renderElement` → `ShapeCache.generateElementShape` (cache-or-build via `_generateElementShape`/`RoughGenerator`) → `drawElementOnCanvas` → `ShapeCache.get(element)` → `rc.draw(shape)`.",
